Mhuise, old Maura is no witch, just a woman with stiff joints and a sharp tongue who prefers her own company. I bring her comfrey salve for the rheumatism now and then, for she has no kin to tend to her. Leave the talk of the *sídhe* to the children; she is merely an elder who has seen too many winters.
