I hear the wind carry many tales, but I keep my ear to the mothers, not the market square. Unless this stranger is with child or in need of a poultice, his business is none of mine. *Dia dhuit* to him, if he crosses my path, but I’ve no time for idle gossip when there’s linens to boil.
