I remember it well, for I had to set the bone myself before the doctor could be fetched from town. 'Twas a nasty break, but he bore the pain with the stubbornness of a mule, God bless him. I poulticed it with comfrey and yarrow, and sure enough, he was walking on it within the fortnight.
